# Use-case 06 pinned bug (claim C2) -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): a reference DEFERS on a
# pending type()/hide() wrapper instead of cloning the call, so
# hide(pack(...)) hides the FIELD m exactly as hide({literal map})
# does, and a downstream pack sourcing from the hidden children emits
# their values. Historically the downstream reference cloned the
# still-pending hide call, the clone resolved at the reference's site
# and stamped hide marks AFTER the reference's mark-clearing walk had
# run -- so the generated children arrived marked and the downstream
# pack emitted them EMPTY, exit 0.
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/marks.tsv hide-pack-field-hidden,
# hide-pack-downstream-pack.
# expected: {"col":...,"out":{"web":{"got":{"a":1}}}} exit 0
# actual:   {"col":...,"out":{"web":{"got":{"a":1}}}} exit 0
col: { web: { a: 1 } }
m: hide(pack($.col, _))
out: pack($.m, { got: _ })
